<div class="section">

<h3>Safety Procedures</h3>

<div class="warning">

<h4>⚠ Before Every Locate</h4>

<ul>

<li>Wear required PPE.</li>

<li>Inspect receiver and transmitter for damage.</li>

<li>Verify battery charge.</li>

<li>Check all test leads for cuts or exposed wire.</li>

<li>Always obtain utility locates before excavation.</li>

<li>Never assume depth readings are exact.</li>

<li>Use caution around energized electrical systems.</li>

</ul>

</div>

</div>

<div class="section">

<h3>Troubleshooting</h3>

<table>

<tr>
<th>Problem</th>
<th>Possible Cause</th>
<th>Solution</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>No Signal</td>
<td>Bad connection</td>
<td>Reconnect leads and verify grounding.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Weak Signal</td>
<td>Low transmitter output</td>
<td>Increase frequency or relocate ground stake.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Erratic Readings</td>
<td>Electrical interference</td>
<td>Reduce gain and move away from interference.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Depth Incorrect</td>
<td>Improper receiver position</td>
<td>Center receiver directly over utility.</td>
</tr>

</table>

</div>

<div class="section">

<h3>Maintenance Checklist</h3>

<ul>

<li>✔ Wipe equipment clean after every use.</li>

<li>✔ Remove dirt from cable connectors.</li>

<li>✔ Replace damaged leads immediately.</li>

<li>✔ Store equipment in carrying case.</li>

<li>✔ Replace batteries when low.</li>

<li>✔ Inspect antenna housing for cracks.</li>

<li>✔ Keep manuals inside carrying case.</li>

</ul>

</div>

<div class="section">

<h3>Douglas Electric Best Practices</h3>

<div class="success">

<ul>

<li>Perform a complete equipment inspection before every locate.</li>

<li>Confirm signal quality before marking utilities.</li>

<li>Cross-check the locate from multiple directions.</li>

<li>Use paint and flags according to company standards.</li>

<li>Document unusual conditions before excavation.</li>

</ul>

</div>

</div>

